# REQUIRES: verilator
# Virtual memories: with --virtual-memories, a registered-read RAM of a folded
# class is kept outside the simulator; a copy issues its reads and writes at
# the state pass and keeps each instance's read data from the responses, and a
# slot whose instance's read is not back waits in a bubble. Against a model of
# the controller (Inputs/tb_vmem.sv), the static simulator matches the target
# at any response latency, with stalled channels and a controller out of room:
# one copy (H stays II when responses come at once), two copies each with its
# own controller, nested sequencers, a short lead, and with --bubbles.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/vmem
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/one --static --virtual-memories ram Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH < %t/one/foldsim_sim.vh
# The read buffer (each instance's read data) reads registered, a host cycle
# early at the instance two ahead, into its output register: block RAM when
# Vivado finds it large enough.
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BUF < %t/one/foldsim_sim.mlir
# BUF: %ram_rdata = seq.firmem 1, 1, old, undefined : <4 x 8, mask 1>
# BUF-NEXT: seq.firmem.write_port %ram_rdata[%vm0_rsp_inst] = %vm0_rsp_data, clock %hostClock enable %vm0_rsp_valid
# BUF-NEXT: [[R:%.+]] = seq.firmem.read_port %ram_rdata[%ahead0_inst2], clock %hostClock
# BUF-NEXT: %ram_rdata_read = seq.firreg [[R]] clock %hostClock
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -Mdir %t/one/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/one/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/one/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/one/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAST
# RUN: %t/one/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/one/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/copies --static --virtual-memories ram --copies Leaf:2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH2 < %t/copies/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DCOPIES2 -DIW=1 -Mdir %t/copies/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/copies/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/copies/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/copies/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=1 +hi=40 +stall=30 +full=10 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/nest --static --virtual-memories ram --nest Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -Mdir %t/nest/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/nest/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/nest/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/nest/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+5 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/short --static --virtual-memories ram --short-lead Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -Mdir %t/short/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/short/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/short/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/short/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+6 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bub --static --virtual-memories ram --bubbles Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/bub/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/bub/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bub/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=30 +bubble=30 +stall=10 | FileCheck %s
# Bubbles at high rates and in long runs, with one copy and with two copies
# under nested sequencers.
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+8 +lo=1 +hi=30 +bubble=95 +burst=16 +stall=10 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bubc --static --virtual-memories ram --copies Leaf:2 --nest --bubbles Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -DCOPIES2 -DIW=1 -Mdir %t/bubc/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/bubc/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bubc/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/bubc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+9 +lo=1 +hi=40 +bubble=90 +burst=8 +stall=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# --min-ii: the frame padded to 40 host cycles (its positions past the
# schedule's idle), a longer distance from each read's request to its use.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/minii --static --modulo --virtual-memories ram --min-ii 40 Leaf > %t/minii.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MINII < %t/minii/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -Mdir %t/minii/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/minii/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/minii/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/minii/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+10 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# The regex is also searched in <class model>:<name> (a copy's by its class):
# Leaf's RAM by its class, in both copies; a class without it keeps it inside.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/cls --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:ram' --copies Leaf:2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH2 < %t/cls/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/other --static --virtual-memories 'Top_model:ram' Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN < %t/other/foldsim_sim.json
# Without --virtual-memories the RAM stays inside.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/plain --static Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN < %t/plain/foldsim_sim.json
# MINII: foldsim-fold-static: II = 40
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 1
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_IW 2
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_AW 4
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_DW 8
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_INSTANCES 4
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_RDWRF 1
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_BASE 64'h0
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_BYTES 64'h1000
# Two copies, two regions of 2 instances x 16 rows x 64 bytes, 4 KiB aligned.
# VH2: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 2
# VH2: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_INSTANCES 2
# VH2: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_BASE 64'h0
# VH2: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_INSTANCES 2
# VH2: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_BASE 64'h1000
# VH2: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_BYTES 64'h2000
# FAST: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles in 2000 host cycles, H 10.00
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
# PLAIN-NOT: "vm0_
